<Page title="Make the decision with evidence." description="Vorbtech’s AI Assurance assessment uses ArtemisKit to examine a declared AI workflow against agreed requirements. The work can cover capability, reliability, security, organisational rules and operational behaviour. You receive scoped technical findings, evidence gaps and recommended next checks, with limitations stated alongside the results." eyebrow="AI Assurance by Vorbtech" faq={faq}><h2>What is AI Assurance?</h2><p>Here, assurance means testing an AI system against the work and boundaries that matter to your organisation. We agree what the system should do, how failure will be recognised, and which evidence is needed to support a decision.</p><h2>What gets assessed?</h2><ul><li><strong>Capability:</strong> Does it complete the defined task?</li><li><strong>Reliability:</strong> What happens with edge cases, repeated attempts and controlled faults?</li><li><strong>Security:</strong> How does it respond to scoped injection, data-exposure and unsafe-action tests?</li><li><strong>Policy adherence:</strong> Does it respect escalation, privacy and approval boundaries?</li><li><strong>Operational behaviour:</strong> What do latency, availability and usage evidence show?</li><li><strong>Evidence quality:</strong> Which observations are valid, incomplete or unavailable?</li></ul><h2>How does an assessment work?</h2><ol><li><strong>Scope:</strong> Agree the workflow, target configuration, authorised data, constraints and success criteria.</li><li><strong>Design:</strong> Define reviewable scenarios and independent checks.</li><li><strong>Execute:</strong> Run controlled tests with declared tools and budgets.</li><li><strong>Review:</strong> Examine findings with technical, risk and domain stakeholders.</li></ol><h2>What do you receive?</h2><p>The agreed scope can include a scenario inventory, sanitised execution evidence, a technical findings report, an executive readout, limitations and prioritised remediation or retesting steps. Deliverables and commercial terms are agreed before work starts.</p><div class="ak-note">Technical evidence supports governance review. It does not certify legal compliance, guarantee safety or replace legal, privacy, security or domain judgment.</div><h2>Can I use the toolkit independently?</h2><p>Yes. The open-source toolkit is available without purchasing an assessment. VIS-led assessment work is a separate engagement.</p><div class="ak-actions"><a class="ak-btn" href="/apply/">Prepare an assessment request ↗</a><a class="ak-btn outline" href="/docs/">Explore the toolkit docs ↗</a></div></Page>
